stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    state "clean" as clean
    state "conflicted" as conflicted

    [*] --> clean: create / repair\nmaterialise base or branch tip

    clean --> clean: snapshot\n(tree already equals the branch)
    clean --> clean: adopt history
    clean --> clean: adopt content\n(materialise the branch tip)
    clean --> conflicted: begin resolution\n(materialise the merge, or jj new theirs ours)
    clean --> conflicted: begin resolution at an introducing commit\n(jj: jj new <conflicted>)

    conflicted --> conflicted: write / patch / bash\n(edits not yet in the VCS)
    conflicted --> conflicted: snapshot, VCS still reports conflicts
    conflicted --> clean: snapshot, VCS reports no conflicts
    conflicted --> clean: abandon\n(materialise the previous tip)

    clean --> [*]: delete

    note right of clean
        The shared branch may have moved. That is a
        branch state, not a tree state: the tree is
        still clean and the branch advance is held.
    end note

    note right of conflicted
        The only signal of "resolution in progress" is
        the VCS's own report for the revision /src
        holds. There is no separate mode flag.
    end note
